# Tamsin Tealeaf's personal quest, The Woman in the Locket (data/quests/the_locket.json,
# docs/story/personal_quests.md). Every scene needs Tamsin: when a custom hero takes his place the quest never starts.
# Started from into_the_mists/arrival:hooks. Her face: village_of_barovia/ireena:locket. Her name: Madam Eva's answer
# (svalich_road/madam_eva:q_locket) or Sergei at the pool (krezk/pool:ireena_vision). The coach: Henrik's confession
# (vallaki/henrik:confess) sets locket_coach_known; the camp talk or Arrigal (vallaki/vistani_camp) turn it into the
# stage. The locket's fate: the Pool of the White Sun (krezk/pool:pool_menu). Castle beats are hooks: see the doc.

# --- Arrigal and the black carriage (vallaki/vistani_camp:arrigal_menu) ---------------------------------------

~ arrigal
set locket_arrigal_confirmed
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: The black carriage. The one with nobody driving. Where does it go when it isn't here?
Arrigal [sly]: Wherever it's sent, little man. Last spring it was sent out through the mists, empty, with the door on the latch and a silver trinket on the seat. My master said a thief would come.
Arrigal: A thief always comes. It's the most reliable thing about the world outside.
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: He left it out. For me. Like milk for a cat.
Arrigal [smile]: Not for you. For whoever came. You were simply the one with the quickest hands and the poorest sense. He was delighted, I hear, when you crossed the border with it. He likes it when a plan arrives on time.
interject name:ilse_varga: He uses couriers who don't know they're couriers. Old trick. Works on the best.
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: Thank you, Ilse. That's very nearly comforting.
if not (quest.the_locket >= the_coach)
quest the_locket the_coach
endif
-> vallaki/vistani_camp:arrigal_menu

# --- The Pool of the White Sun (krezk/pool:pool_menu) ------------------------------------------------------------

~ pool
Narrator: Tamsin takes out the locket and opens it over the water. The little painted woman looks up at the sky in the pool.
Narrator: Beside Tamsin's reflection there is a second one, though nobody stands beside him: a young man in an old coat with a sunburst at the breast, looking at the locket with an expression nobody should have to wear for three hundred years.
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: Oh. Hello. You'll be the S. I've been carrying your post. Badly. I've been reading it.
Sergei von Zarovich: I gave it to her on a spring morning, at this water. She wore it the day she fell. My brother took it from the gorge, and he has used it as bait ever since.
Sergei von Zarovich: You needn't give it to me. It isn't mine any more. It is yours, or hers, or his, depending on what you do next.
* [name:tamsin_tealeaf] (Drop the locket into the pool.) -> pool_sergei
* [name:tamsin_tealeaf] [if guest:ireena] (Put the locket in Ireena's hand.) -> pool_ireena
* [name:tamsin_tealeaf] (Close it, and keep it.) -> pool_keep

~ pool_sergei
set locket_fate = "pool"
quest the_locket given_to_sergei
Narrator: Tamsin holds it out over the water a long moment, the way a man holds out the last good thing he owns. Then he lets go.
Narrator: It doesn't sink. A hand comes up out of the reflection, not out of the water, and closes round it, and it is gone.
Sergei von Zarovich: Thank you, thief. You are the first person in a very long time to steal something back for her.
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: Returned. It's called returning. I'm told it's very rewarding. ...It is, actually. Huh.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Mm. You'll sleep tonight. Properly. I'd put money on it, if I gambled.
interject name:ilse_varga: She gambles. Badly.
-> krezk/pool:pool_menu

~ pool_ireena
set locket_fate = "ireena"
quest the_locket given_to_ireena
Narrator: Tamsin closes the locket and puts it in Ireena's palm, and folds her fingers over it with his.
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: It's yours. I think it always was. I just carried it, like a parcel. Very well paid parcel, emotionally.
Ireena [sad]: I don't know whose it ought to be. Hers. Mine. I'll keep it until I know.
Sergei von Zarovich: Keep it out of my brother's sight, Ireena. He wants it to remind you. Let it remind you of me instead.
Ireena: ...I remember a chapel full of white flowers. I'll keep that one.
-> krezk/pool:pool_menu

~ pool_keep
set locket_fate = "kept"
if not (quest.the_locket >= kept)
quest the_locket kept
endif
Narrator: Tamsin snaps the locket shut and puts it back inside his shirt, where it sits over his heart like a stone that's been in the sun.
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: Not yet. I'm a thief. We don't give things back the first time someone asks nicely. It's a professional standard.
Sergei von Zarovich: Then carry her carefully. My brother will ask for her too, and he will not ask nicely.
-> krezk/pool:pool_menu
